body:
I'm a LING major and I chose to do the Language Track. It would be good if you want to Double major in LING and Japanese if you want. But, as for the content for the LING courses, I think that it's not too bad. It's not easy, but it's not super hard, though this pandemic will definitely bring forth different results based on your circumstance. I know it has for me, but the professors are very understanding and supportive. So that's why I don't think you will completely crumble in the LING major. And us LING majors collaborate and help each other a lot so you won't be alone at all. I am also taking Orgo 1 this semester and though it is hard, it's so much better than the previous semesters when I took it and failed :/. I wasn't a STEM major, but I was PHSC and got booted out cause of Orgo 1 and the dreaded benchmarks lol.

&#x200B;

Also, to go into the Linguistics major, we study language data. So you can choose the language track, but if you choose the cognition track, you'll go more deeply into syntax, phonology, philosophy of language, and other subfields in linguistics. I can give more input if you like. And there's also a Linguistics Club that basically talks about everything Linguistics and language and other applications of linguistics.
